{"kind":"request","text":"CUT-A2: the register script never widens the installed list by\ndefault.\n\nThe fact at main 0ad4aa91. `scripts/register-values.mjs` without\n`--only` keeps the old primary root and writes\n`INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES` with both roots, also in a file that\nhad no list. A listed root admits creation chains\n(`packages/scope/src/creation-lineage.ts:143`). The first head A\n(f8c71ba2) so listed a retired register on two Workers, and the\nchecker refused it (0ee19578). The checker's review of CUT-A\n(1ee6b387) names two smaller points.\n\nWork, in one small head:\n\n1. The script requires one of two flags and refuses with neither:\n   `--only` writes the new root alone, and `--keep` keeps each\n   listed root and adds the new one. The refusal names both flags.\n2. The script keeps the mode of the file that it replaces.\n3. `docs/deploy.md` states the two flags, and says in one sentence\n   that a listed root admits creation under that root. The runbook\n   names the cleanup when a run dies and leaves the pending\n   directory beside the file.\n4. Tests in `scripts/register-values.test.mjs`: the refusal with\n   neither flag, each flag on a file with a list and on a file\n   without one, and the kept mode.\n\nOrder: after head A and R1. It holds nothing. One gate, or the\nfollow-up rule when it fits.","body":{"conditions":"scripts/register-values.mjs refuses a call with neither --only nor --keep, keeps the file mode, and its tests cover both flags on a file with a list and without one. docs/deploy.md states the flags and the cleanup. Gate passes and the checker reviews the head.","target_head":"0ad4aa9102fe5f75b692d3adb30c8b00a6914574","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}